   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion to recommit with instructions Failed by recorded vote: 196 - 230 (Roll no. 527).",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8A000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "15:05:33",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question on the motion to recommit with instructions was ordered without objection. (consideration: CR H8101)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:56:21",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the E. B. Johnson (TX) motion to recommit with instructions, pending reservation of a point order. The instructions contained in the motion seek to report the same back to the House forthwith with an amendment to exempt any Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) regulation that protects communities in an emergency, including an Ebola or pandemic flu outbreak, the release of toxic chemicals, or a nuclear, biological, or terrorist attack. Subsequently, the reservation of a point of order was removed.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H36100",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:55:53",
   "committees": [
    {
     "name": "Science, Space, and Technology Committee",
     "systemCode": "hssy00",
     "url": "https://api.congress.gov/v3/committee/house/hssy00?format=json"
    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Ms. Johnson, E. B. moved to recommit with instructions to the Committee on Science, Space, and Technology. (consideration: CR H8100-8102; text: CR H8100-8101)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H34400",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:54:33",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House adopted the amendment in the nature of a substitute as agreed to by the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union. (text of amendment in the nature of a substitute: CR H8097)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:54:17",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule. (consideration: CR H8100)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32600",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:53:32",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House rose from the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union to report H.R. 4012.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:15:43",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H. Res. 756, the House proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Kennedy Part B amendment No. 2.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "14:07:39",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H. Res. 756, the House proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Gosar Part B amendment No. 1.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "13:10:31",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - The Committee of the Whole proceeded with one hour of general debate on H.R. 4012.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32400",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "13:10:16",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Speaker designated the Honorable John J. Duncan, Jr. to act as Chairman of the Committee.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32020",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "13:10:15",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "House resolved itself into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union pursuant to H. Res. 756 and Rule XVIII.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "13:09:38",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1422, H.R. 4012 and H.R. 4795. General debate is limited to 1 hour for each bill. The resolution specifies certain amendments are in order for H.R. 1422, H.R. 4012, and H.R. 4795. One motion to recommit with instructions is permitted for each bill.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-19",
   "actionTime": "13:09:33",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 756. (consideration: CR H8087-8103)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "2014-11-17",
   "actionTime": "19:26:47",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 756 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1422, H.R. 4012 and H.R. 4795. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 1422, H.R. 4012, and H.R. 4795. General debate is limited to 1 hour for each bill. The resolution specifies certain amendments are in order for H.R. 1422, H.R. 4012, and H.R. 4795. One motion to recommit with instructions is permitted for each bill.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
